# Assets

Rules for files under `app/assets/`. Follow global rules in `global.mdc` for formatting and project conventions.

## Purpose

The `assets/` directory holds **processed static files** bundled by Nuxt/Vite: global styles, fonts, icons, and images. Files here are imported in app code; use `public/` for assets that must keep a fixed URL without processing.

## Directory Structure

```
app/assets/
├── styles/
│   ├── app.scss                 # Global style entry point
│   ├── base/                    # Variables, typography, resets, animations
│   │   ├── _variables.scss
│   │   ├── _typography.scss
│   │   ├── _containers.scss
│   │   ├── _framework.scss
│   │   ├── _animations.scss
│   │   └── index.scss
│   ├── utils/                   # Mixins and helper classes
│   │   ├── _mixins.scss
│   │   ├── _helpers.scss
│   │   └── index.scss
│   ├── layouts/                 # Layout/shell styles (navbar, tabs, overlays)
│   ├── components/              # Reusable UI partials (buttons, cards, forms, tables)
│   ├── pages/                   # Page-specific styles (auth, profile, settings)
│   └── vendors/                 # Third-party overrides (e.g. SweetAlert)
├── icons/
│   └── css/all.min.css          # Icon font / icon library CSS
├── fonts/                       # Self-hosted font files (woff, woff2, ttf)
└── img/
    ├── auth/                    # Auth illustrations (login.svg, register.svg)
    ├── icons/                   # UI icons (location-pin.svg, etc.)
    ├── no-data-img.svg          # Shared empty-state illustration
    └── loader.svg               # Loading placeholder
```

| Folder | Contents |
|--------|----------|
| `styles/` | SCSS/CSS source organized by layer |
| `fonts/` | Web fonts referenced from `_typography.scss` |
| `icons/` | Vendor icon CSS or custom icon assets |
| `img/` | SVG/PNG/GIF illustrations and UI imagery |

## Styles Architecture

### Entry point

Import one global stylesheet from a Nuxt plugin or `nuxt.config.ts`:

```ts
import '~/assets/styles/app.scss'
import '~/assets/icons/css/all.min.css'
```

`app.scss` composes layers in order:

```scss
@use '../../node_modules/vuetify/lib/styles/main.sass';

@use 'base/index' as base;
@use 'utils/index' as utils;
@use 'layouts/index' as layouts;
@use 'components/index' as components;
@use 'pages/index' as pages;
@use 'vendors/index' as vendors;
```

**Layer order:** base → utils → layouts → components → pages → vendors.

### Partials and indexes

- Prefix partial files with **`_`** (`_variables.scss`, `_buttons.scss`).
- Each folder has an **`index.scss`** that `@use`s its partials.
- Use **`@use`**, not `@import`, for internal modules.
- Reference variables/mixins with namespaces or `@use '...' as *`:

```scss
@use '../base/variables' as *;
@use '../utils/mixins' as *;

.btn {
  border-radius: 0.5rem;
}
```

### Layer responsibilities

| Layer | Scope |
|-------|--------|
| `base/` | SCSS variables, typography, `@font-face`, global resets, scrollbars |
| `utils/` | Mixins (`absolute-overlay`, breakpoints) and utility classes |
| `layouts/` | App shell: navbar, tabs, side columns, overlays |
| `components/` | Buttons, cards, forms, modals, tables, notifications |
| `pages/` | Styles scoped to specific routes (auth, profile, download) |
| `vendors/` | Overrides for third-party libraries |

- Put styles in the **lowest appropriate layer** — page-specific rules in `pages/`, shared UI in `components/`.
- Do not add one-off page styles to `base/` or `app.scss`.

### Variables

Define design tokens in `base/_variables.scss`:

```scss
$primary: #00bfb3;
$secondary: #00a6ed;
$background: #f5f9ff;
$text-color: #374355;
```

- Use variables for colors, shadows, and shared sizes.
- Prefer theme/CSS custom properties when integrating with a UI framework (Vuetify, Nuxt UI).

### RTL support

Wrap direction-sensitive rules in RTL ignore comments when needed:

```scss
/*!rtl:begin:ignore*/
left: 0 !important;
right: initial !important;
/*!rtl:end:ignore*/
```

## Images

- Store illustrations and UI graphics under `img/`, grouped by feature (`img/auth/`, `img/icons/`).
- Reference in templates with the **`~/assets/`** alias:

```vue
<v-img src="~/assets/img/no-data-img.svg" />
<v-img src="~/assets/img/auth/login.svg" />
```

- Use **SVG** for icons and illustrations when possible.
- Reuse shared assets (`no-data-img.svg`, `loader.svg`) across pages and components.
- Use descriptive, kebab-case filenames (`no-data-img.svg`, `green-logo.svg`).

## Fonts

- Place font files in `assets/fonts/`.
- Declare `@font-face` in `base/_typography.scss` with woff2/woff/ttf fallbacks.
- Reference family names consistently in typography and theme config.

## Icons

- Vendor icon CSS (e.g. Font Awesome) lives under `assets/icons/css/`.
- Import icon CSS once in the app plugin alongside global styles.
- Prefer icon components or the UI library’s icon set for new work; add vendor CSS only when the project already depends on it.

## `assets/` vs `public/`

| Location | Use for |
|----------|---------|
| `app/assets/` | Styles, fonts, images imported in Vue/TS, Vite-processed files |
| `public/` | `robots.txt`, favicons, files needing a fixed root URL (`/file.pdf`) |

## Naming Conventions

- **SCSS partials:** `_kebab-case.scss`
- **Images:** `kebab-case.svg` / `.png`
- **Folders:** plural or feature name (`fonts/`, `img/auth/`, `styles/components/`)

## What Not to Put in Assets

- Vue components (use `app/components/`).
- API logic or JSON config.
- Windows metadata files (`*.Zone.Identifier`) — exclude from the repo.
- Duplicate copies of the same image under multiple paths.
- Large unoptimized binaries when SVG or compression is sufficient.

## Adding New Assets

### New global style partial

1. Add `_my-feature.scss` in the correct layer folder.
2. `@use` it from that folder’s `index.scss`.
3. Keep variables in `base/`, mixins in `utils/`.

### New image

1. Save under `app/assets/img/{feature}/`.
2. Reference as `~/assets/img/{feature}/{name}.svg` in templates.
3. Reuse existing empty-state/loader assets before adding new ones.

### New page-specific styles

1. Create `styles/pages/_my-page.scss`.
2. Register in `styles/pages/index.scss`.
3. Scope selectors to a page class (e.g. `.page-wrapper`, `.auth-page`) to avoid leaks.

## Nuxt UI / Tailwind Projects

When using Nuxt UI + Tailwind (e.g. `app/assets/css/main.css`), keep framework imports in the CSS entry:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "@nuxt/ui";

@theme static {
  --font-sans: 'Public Sans', sans-serif;
}
```

- Extend theme tokens in `@theme` rather than scattering magic values in components.
- Add SCSS layers under `app/assets/styles/` only when the project adopts SCSS alongside Tailwind.
